# ---- 689 Cloud Computing ----
H("689.d.1.A",3,"A start-up avoids buying servers and instead rents computing power by the hour. One benefit of this move is:","paying only for what it uses",["owning all the hardware","never needing the internet","guaranteed zero downtime"],"Pay-as-you-go lowers upfront cost.")
H("689.d.1.A",4,"A risk a company accepts when moving its data to a cloud provider is:","depending on the provider's availability and security",["having to buy more cables","losing all internet access","being unable to scale"],"Providers become a dependency.")
H("689.d.1.B",3,"Renting virtual servers, storage and networks from a provider is called:","infrastructure as a service (IaaS)",["software as a service","a desktop suite","a local network"],"IaaS supplies raw computing resources.")
H("689.d.1.B",4,"Using a web-based email service you do not install or maintain is an example of:","software as a service (SaaS)",["infrastructure as a service","a private data center","on-premises hosting"],"SaaS delivers finished applications.")
H("689.d.1.C",3,"A school wants a cloud plan for a yearbook site that is busy only in May. The plan should expect:","seasonal spikes in usage and cost",["constant flat usage","no usage at all","unlimited free service"],"Usage plans reflect demand patterns.")
H("689.d.1.C",4,"In a case-study usage plan, estimating monthly storage, compute hours and data transfer helps the business to:","predict its cloud bill",["avoid backups","skip security","choose a logo"],"Estimates become cost forecasts.")
H("689.d.1.D",3,"A cloud region is best described as:","a geographic area containing cloud data centers",["a single hard drive","a billing account","a type of password"],"Regions are locations of facilities.")
H("689.d.1.D",4,"An edge location mainly exists to:","cache content closer to users for faster delivery",["store all billing data","train new employees","replace regions entirely"],"Edge sites reduce latency.")
H("689.d.1.E",3,"Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud are each a:","major cloud computing provider",["web browser","programming language","operating system"],"They are leading cloud platforms.")
H("689.d.1.E",4,"When comparing cloud providers for a school project, a team should weigh price, services offered and:","support and data location options",["the provider's logo","the length of the name","the color of the website"],"Comparison uses practical criteria.")
H("689.d.2.A",3,"A cloud service that stores files and lets you open them from any device provides:","object or file storage",["a printer driver","a game console","a power supply"],"Cloud storage syncs across devices.")
H("689.d.2.A",4,"A managed database service is useful because the provider handles:","patching, backups and hardware upkeep",["writing your queries","choosing your data","designing your logo"],"Managed services reduce admin work.")
H("689.d.2.B",3,"A cloud console is a web interface used to:","create and manage cloud resources",["print documents","edit photos","play videos"],"Consoles control services.")
H("689.d.2.B",4,"In a console, a beginner who wants to start a virtual server would look for the service that provides:","compute instances",["only billing statements","only email","only fonts"],"Compute services launch servers.")
H("689.d.2.C",3,"A streaming video company uses the cloud to handle:","millions of viewers at the same time",["only one viewer","only paper records","a single office"],"Cloud scales for large audiences.")
H("689.d.2.C",4,"A hospital storing scans in the cloud must still follow rules about:","protecting patient privacy",["font choices","wallpaper","emoji use"],"Healthcare data has privacy laws.")
H("689.d.2.D",3,"The domain name system (DNS) turns a name like example.com into a:","numeric IP address",["password","file size","screen color"],"DNS translates names to addresses.")
H("689.d.2.D",4,"If DNS is not working, a user may still reach a site by typing its:","IP address directly",["email password","favorite color","username"],"The numeric address bypasses name lookup.")
H("689.d.2.E",3,"An object storage bucket is a container used to hold:","files such as images and documents",["only passwords","only processors","only monitors"],"Buckets store objects.")
H("689.d.2.E",4,"Bucket names in many cloud services must be:","unique within the service",["blank","a single letter only","identical to others"],"Global uniqueness avoids conflicts.")
H("689.d.2.F",3,"A content delivery network (CDN) makes websites faster by:","serving copies of content from servers near the visitor",["deleting images","slowing the server","blocking visitors"],"Nearby copies reduce delay.")
H("689.d.2.F",4,"A CDN also helps a site survive a traffic surge because it:","spreads requests across many servers",["shuts the site down","adds more ads","lowers image quality only"],"Distribution relieves the origin.")
H("689.d.2.G",3,"To speed up a site with a CDN distribution, an admin points the distribution at the site's:","origin (the source of its content)",["email list","paper menu","tax records"],"The origin supplies the files.")
H("689.d.2.G",4,"After attaching a distribution to a website, visitors should reach the site through the distribution's:","domain or alias name",["old password","backup file","billing page"],"The new endpoint routes through edge locations.")
H("689.d.2.H",3,"Block storage works like a:","hard drive attached to a server",["printed book","video call","text message"],"Blocks act as disk volumes.")
H("689.d.2.H",4,"Compared with object storage, block storage is better for:","an operating system or database that needs fast disk access",["storing billions of backups cheaply","hosting a static photo gallery","archiving old documents"],"Low-latency volumes suit active workloads.")
H("689.d.2.I",3,"A company needs to keep seven years of old records at the lowest cost, rarely opened. The best choice is:","archival storage",["fast block storage","a local USB drive only","a database cache"],"Archival tiers are cheapest for rare access.")
H("689.d.2.I",4,"A busy database needs very fast reads and writes. The best virtual storage is:","high-performance block storage",["cold archive storage","a static website bucket","a printed ledger"],"Active databases need low latency.")
H("689.d.2.J",3,"Before using a new block storage volume, an admin must choose its size and:","the availability zone it lives in",["its favorite color","its shoe size","its username"],"Volumes belong to a zone.")
H("689.d.2.J",4,"A block storage volume created in one availability zone cannot normally be attached to a server in:","a different availability zone",["the same availability zone","the same region and zone","its own zone"],"Zone boundaries limit attachment.")
H("689.d.2.K",3,"Attaching a volume to a virtual computing instance makes the volume:","available to the instance as a disk",["disappear","a printer","a website"],"Attachment connects storage to compute.")
H("689.d.2.K",4,"After attaching a new volume, the instance's operating system usually still must:","format and mount the volume before use",["delete the volume","change the region","rename the cloud"],"A blank disk needs a file system.")
H("689.d.2.L",3,"A simple website on a virtual computing instance needs web server software and:","the site's files",["a game controller","a printer","a camera"],"The server must serve content.")
H("689.d.2.L",4,"To let visitors reach the instance's website, the instance's firewall rules must allow inbound:","web traffic on the HTTP/HTTPS ports",["no traffic at all","only printer traffic","only email traffic"],"Ports must be open for browsers.")
H("689.d.3.A",3,"A best practice for identity and access management (IAM) is giving each user:","only the permissions needed for their job",["every permission","none of the permissions","the owner's password"],"Least privilege reduces risk.")
H("689.d.3.A",4,"Turning on multi-factor authentication for IAM users helps protect accounts if a:","password is stolen",["screen is dim","fan is loud","mouse is slow"],"A second factor blocks stolen passwords.")
H("689.d.3.B",3,"Strong cloud security matters to society because breaches of cloud-stored data can expose many people's:","personal information",["wallpaper","playlist colors","desk setups"],"Breaches harm individuals.")
H("689.d.3.B",4,"As more schools and hospitals rely on cloud services, a major societal concern is protecting:","privacy and trust in digital records",["font styles","screensavers","emoji sets"],"Trust depends on security.")
H("689.d.3.C",3,"In cloud security, a user is:","an identity for a person or app that can sign in",["a firewall","a storage price","a region"],"Users are identities.")
H("689.d.3.C",4,"A policy in cloud security is a document that:","defines which actions are allowed or denied",["draws a network map","lists user birthdays","prints invoices"],"Policies set permissions.")
H("689.d.3.D",3,"After a scan finds an outdated web server, the first step in a vulnerability process is to:","identify and rank the risk",["delete the server","ignore it","announce passwords"],"Assess before fixing.")
H("689.d.3.D",4,"Applying a patch and then rescanning a web server is done to:","confirm the vulnerability is fixed",["add more bugs","slow the site","remove logs"],"Verification closes the loop.")
H("689.d.3.E",3,"A cloud security lapse such as a publicly open storage bucket is best fixed by:","restricting access to authorized users",["making it larger","renaming it only","adding more files"],"Closing public access stops exposure.")
H("689.d.3.E",4,"After a security lapse is fixed, a team should also review logs to learn:","whether anyone accessed the data",["what to rename the bucket","how to change fonts","which logo to use"],"Logs show if data was exposed.")
H("689.d.3.F",3,"A company wants to block common web attacks like SQL injection on its site. It should choose a:","web application firewall",["file backup service","video encoder","email client"],"A WAF filters malicious requests.")
H("689.d.3.F",4,"A team needs to detect unusual login behavior across accounts. The best cloud service type is:","threat detection monitoring",["image resizing","DNS hosting","file compression"],"Threat detection flags anomalies.")
H("689.d.3.G",3,"A text alert for a suspicious IAM event is often sent through a:","notification service",["printer","spreadsheet","calculator"],"Notification services send messages.")
H("689.d.3.G",4,"To be alerted when someone signs in as the root user, an admin sets up an event rule that triggers a:","text message notification",["system reboot","file deletion","price change"],"Rules connect events to alerts.")
H("689.d.3.H",3,"Monitoring services mainly show:","how resources are performing right now",["old tax forms","family photos","menu options"],"Monitoring tracks metrics.")
H("689.d.3.H",4,"Logging services differ from monitoring in that logs mainly record:","a detailed history of events and actions",["only the current CPU number","only storage prices","only user birthdays"],"Logs keep records for review.")
H("689.d.4.A",3,"A system that records thousands of small bank deposits as they happen is built for:","online transactional processing (OLTP)",["online analytical processing","video editing","image printing"],"OLTP handles many small transactions.")
H("689.d.4.A",4,"A system that scans years of sales data to find trends is built for:","online analytical processing (OLAP)",["transactional entry","name lookups","password resets"],"OLAP supports analysis of large data sets.")
H("689.d.4.B",3,"Caching data helps an application because frequently used data is kept:","in a fast place close to the app",["offline forever","on paper","in a locked safe"],"Caches shorten access time.")
H("689.d.4.B",4,"A cache can also lower costs by reducing the number of:","slow requests to the main database",["users","passwords","pixels"],"Fewer database hits save resources.")
H("689.d.4.C",3,"A load balancer attached to a web page sends each visitor to:","one of several healthy servers",["the same broken server","a printer","nowhere"],"It distributes traffic.")
H("689.d.4.C",4,"To attach a load balancer, an admin registers the web servers as its:","targets",["passwords","logos","invoices"],"Targets receive forwarded requests.")
H("689.d.4.D",3,"One benefit of load balancing is that if a server fails, traffic:","is routed to the remaining servers",["stops completely","doubles the bill","is deleted"],"Health checks reroute traffic.")
H("689.d.4.D",4,"Load balancing improves availability because no single server:","has to carry all the visitors",["is ever turned on","is ever updated","is ever monitored"],"Spreading load prevents overload.")
H("689.d.4.E",3,"To evaluate a load balancer's performance, an admin reviews metrics such as:","request count and response time",["office hours","paper usage","font size"],"Metrics show how it behaves.")
H("689.d.4.E",4,"If a load balancer's response time keeps rising during busy hours, the admin should consider:","adding more servers behind it",["deleting its logs","removing health checks","closing the console"],"More capacity eases load.")
H("689.d.4.F",3,"Platform as a service (PaaS) lets a developer build an app without managing:","the underlying servers and operating system",["any code","any ideas","any users"],"PaaS hides infrastructure.")
H("689.d.4.F",4,"A developer deploys a web app by uploading code to a PaaS. The platform then handles:","scaling and running the app",["writing the code","choosing the colors","naming the company"],"The platform runs the code.")
H("689.d.4.G",3,"Infrastructure as code means building cloud resources using:","text templates that describe them",["screwdrivers","paper forms","phone calls"],"Templates define infrastructure.")
H("689.d.4.G",4,"A benefit of using a template to build a virtual private cloud (VPC) is that it:","creates the same network again and again reliably",["makes each network different","needs no testing","skips security"],"Templates are repeatable.")
H("689.d.5.A",3,"Machine learning is a method in which computers:","learn patterns from data to make predictions",["follow only fixed rules","need no data","cannot improve"],"ML learns from examples.")
H("689.d.5.A",4,"One societal concern about machine learning systems is that they can:","reflect bias found in their training data",["always be perfectly fair","never make errors","run without electricity"],"Biased data leads to biased results.")
H("689.d.5.B",3,"A farm uses cloud-connected sensors to water crops only when soil is dry. This is an emerging-technology use case called:","the Internet of Things (IoT)",["a floppy disk","a word processor","a paper log"],"IoT devices report data to the cloud.")
H("689.d.5.B",4,"A store uses cloud AI to predict which products will sell out next week. The use case is:","demand forecasting",["font design","wallpaper choice","typing practice"],"Forecasting uses cloud-scale analysis.")
H("689.d.5.C",3,"A value proposition of the cloud for a small business is that it can:","use powerful tools without buying hardware",["avoid all risk","skip planning","stop paying forever"],"Cloud lowers entry cost.")
H("689.d.5.C",4,"Assessing the value of moving to the cloud means comparing its benefits against its:","costs and risks",["font options","logos","desk sizes"],"Value is net benefit.")
H("689.d.5.D",3,"A cloud service that scans stored files for sensitive data like credit card numbers helps to:","analyze and protect data",["print posters","edit audio","design logos"],"Data-protection services find exposures.")
H("689.d.5.D",4,"A cloud network service that watches traffic and flags unusual patterns helps to:","manage and secure networks",["bake bread","grade quizzes","choose colors"],"Network tools monitor and protect.")
H("689.d.5.E",3,"Blockchain is a shared record that stores data in linked:","blocks that are hard to change",["paper folders","erasable notes","private diaries"],"Blocks are chained with hashes.")
H("689.d.5.E",4,"A benefit of blockchain is that a recorded transaction is:","very difficult to alter without detection",["easy for anyone to erase","hidden from all parties","random each time"],"Immutability builds trust.")
H("689.d.5.F",3,"A cloud development kit lets developers describe cloud infrastructure using:","a familiar programming language",["finger paint","paper maps","sound waves"],"Kits turn code into resources.")
H("689.d.5.F",4,"A software development kit (SDK) for a cloud service mainly provides:","libraries and tools to call the service from code",["office furniture","hardware cables","printer paper"],"SDKs simplify service use.")
H("689.d.5.G",3,"A software development framework can model an application's resources and then:","provision them in the cloud automatically",["delete them at random","ignore them","print them"],"Frameworks generate templates and deploy.")
H("689.d.5.G",4,"Before provisioning a modeled application, the framework can show a preview so the developer can:","review the changes it will make",["hide the changes","skip the review","remove the preview"],"Previews prevent surprises.")
H("689.d.6.A",3,"In the shared responsibility model, the provider is responsible for:","security of the cloud infrastructure itself",["the customer's passwords","the customer's data choices","the customer's staff training"],"Providers secure facilities and hardware.")
H("689.d.6.A",4,"In the shared responsibility model, the customer is responsible for:","security in the cloud, such as access settings and data",["the provider's buildings","the provider's power grid","the provider's hardware"],"Customers configure their own use.")
H("689.d.6.B",3,"Who is responsible for deciding which employees can open a company's cloud storage bucket?","the customer",["the data center electricians","the hardware vendor","the internet provider"],"Access settings belong to the customer.")
H("689.d.6.B",4,"Who is responsible for physical security of the data center buildings?","the cloud provider",["the customer's interns","the customer's website visitors","the domain registrar"],"Providers secure facilities.")
H("689.d.6.C",3,"The shared model reduces the risk of a stolen password leading to a breach because the customer can:","enforce multi-factor authentication",["buy new servers","change cable colors","rename regions"],"Customers control sign-in rules.")
H("689.d.6.C",4,"A common cloud threat is misconfiguration. The shared model makes it the customer's job to:","review and correct their own settings",["rebuild the provider's data center","replace the provider's hardware","rewrite the internet"],"Misconfiguration is on the customer's side.")
H("689.d.6.D",3,"When an automated security alert fires, the first step is usually to:","review the alert details to understand what happened",["ignore it","delete all data","shut down the internet"],"Understand before acting.")
H("689.d.6.D",4,"After confirming an alert is real, an admin should contain the problem, fix the cause and then:","document what was done",["hide the alert","disable all alerts","blame a user"],"Documentation supports learning.")
H("689.d.6.E",3,"An instance in the state 'pending' is:","starting up and not yet ready",["permanently deleted","fully stopped","being billed as terminated"],"Pending precedes running.")
H("689.d.6.E",4,"An instance that has been shut down permanently and cannot be restarted is in the state:","terminated",["pending","running","stopping"],"Terminated instances are gone.")
H("689.d.6.F",3,"A normal launch sequence for an instance moves from pending to:","running",["terminated","stopped","shutting down"],"Launch ends in running.")
H("689.d.6.F",4,"To go from stopped back to running, an instance passes through:","pending",["terminated","deleted","archived"],"Starting again goes through pending.")
H("689.d.6.G",3,"For many providers, a stopped instance does not incur compute charges, but its attached storage:","may still be billed",["is free forever","vanishes","becomes a printer"],"Volumes keep costing money.")
H("689.d.6.G",4,"A running instance is billed for:","the compute time it runs",["only the time it is stopped","nothing at all","only its name"],"Running time is billable.")
H("689.d.6.H",3,"A test server is needed only during work hours. The cost-efficient plan is to:","stop it outside work hours",["keep it running all night","terminate it every day","leave it pending"],"Stopping saves compute charges.")
H("689.d.6.H",4,"A server will never be needed again. The most cost-efficient state is:","terminated",["running","stopped","pending"],"Termination removes all charges.")
H("689.d.7.A",3,"A static website is hosted by storing its HTML, CSS and image files in:","a storage bucket configured for website hosting",["a printer queue","a phone case","an email draft"],"Buckets can serve static files.")
H("689.d.7.A",4,"When setting up a static site in a bucket, the admin must set an index document, which is the:","default page visitors see first",["admin's password","server's brand","billing address"],"The index page is the entry point.")
H("689.d.7.B",3,"A dynamic website differs from a static website because it:","builds pages using code and data when requested",["never changes","has only one page","has no images"],"Dynamic pages are generated.")
H("689.d.7.B",4,"A site that shows each visitor their own account balance after login must be:","dynamic",["static","printed","hand-delivered"],"Personalized content needs server logic.")
H("689.d.7.C",3,"Creating a CDN distribution for a website's bucket helps visitors worldwide get:","faster load times",["slower load times","no pages","more passwords"],"Edge caching speeds delivery.")
H("689.d.7.C",4,"After creating the distribution, the site's address should be updated to use:","the distribution's domain name",["a random number","the old password","a blank page"],"Traffic must flow through the CDN.")
H("689.d.7.D",3,"To launch a dynamic web server on a virtual instance, an admin installs:","web server and application software",["video games","music apps","photo filters"],"The instance needs software to run the site.")
H("689.d.7.D",4,"For visitors to reach the dynamic server, it needs a public IP address and:","a security rule allowing web traffic",["no network","a blocked firewall","a dead port"],"Network access must be opened.")
H("689.d.7.E",3,"A serverless compute function runs code:","only when triggered, without managing servers",["all day, every day","only on paper","only on local laptops"],"Serverless runs on demand.")
H("689.d.7.E",4,"With serverless compute, billing is usually based on:","how many times and how long the function runs",["the color of the code","the number of files in a folder","the size of the office"],"Pay per execution.")
H("689.d.7.F",3,"Auto scaling automatically changes the number of instances based on:","demand",["the weather","paper supply","office hours"],"Scaling follows load.")
H("689.d.7.F",4,"An auto scaling group can keep a minimum number of healthy instances by:","replacing instances that fail health checks",["deleting all instances","turning off monitoring","ignoring failures"],"Self-healing keeps capacity.")
H("689.d.7.G",3,"A launch template for auto scaling stores settings such as the instance type and:","the machine image to launch",["office phone number","coffee orders","paper sizes"],"Templates define what is launched.")
H("689.d.7.G",4,"An auto scaling group needs a minimum, a maximum and a:","desired number of instances",["favorite color","guest list","slogan"],"Capacity boundaries guide scaling.")
H("689.d.7.H",3,"A plan for monitoring an auto scaling group should include tracking:","CPU use and instance counts",["office temperature only","staff birthdays","paper stock"],"Metrics show scaling behavior.")
H("689.d.7.H",4,"Setting an alarm that triggers when CPU use stays high is part of:","a monitoring plan for scaling",["a fonts review","a color study","a menu design"],"Alarms drive scaling actions.")
H("689.d.8.A",3,"Big data refers to data sets so large or fast-changing that they need:","special tools to store and analyze them",["only a pencil","no storage","a calculator only"],"Big data exceeds normal tools.")
H("689.d.8.A",4,"A retailer analyzing millions of purchases to stock shelves better is using big data in the:","retail industry",["agriculture only","forestry only","none of the industries"],"Retail uses data for planning.")
H("689.d.8.B",3,"A benefit of big data in healthcare is spotting:","patterns that help predict disease outbreaks",["nothing useful","only logos","only colors"],"Trends help public health.")
H("689.d.8.B",4,"A risk of collecting huge amounts of personal data is:","privacy loss if the data is misused or breached",["lower storage costs","fewer users","faster typing"],"Large data sets raise privacy stakes.")
H("689.d.8.C",3,"Blockchain makes each new block include a value from the previous block, so changing an old block would:","break the chain and be noticed",["go unnoticed","fix itself","delete the network"],"Linked hashes expose tampering.")
H("689.d.8.C",4,"In a blockchain, many participants hold copies of the ledger, which helps validate transactions because:","they must agree before a block is accepted",["only one person decides","nobody checks","copies are secret"],"Consensus ensures validity.")
H("689.d.8.D",3,"A benefit of blockchain for tracking food shipments is a:","shared, trusted record of each step",["private diary","erasable note","random guess"],"Traceability builds trust.")
H("689.d.8.D",4,"A risk of blockchain business applications is that they can:","use large amounts of energy or be hard to scale",["be too transparent for laws always","need no computers","cost nothing ever"],"Some chains are resource intensive.")

# ---- 690 User Experience (UX) Design I ----
H("690.d.1.A",3,"A UX designer presenting to executives instead of to teenage users should revise the presentation to match the:","audience",["font brand","laptop model","room temperature"],"Presentations must fit who is listening.")
H("690.d.1.A",4,"A design review meant to win approval for funding differs from one meant to teach a team. The designer adjusts for each presentation's:","purpose",["slide count rule","clicker brand","file extension"],"Purpose shapes content and tone.")
H("690.d.1.B",3,"A designer shows a chart of how many users finished checkout and explains in plain words what it means. This is:","interpreting and communicating data clearly",["hiding results","guessing outcomes","avoiding feedback"],"Data must be explained, not just shown.")
H("690.d.1.B",4,"When reporting an observation like 'three users hesitated at the Pay button,' a designer should be:","specific and factual about what was seen",["vague","exaggerated","silent"],"Clear observations support decisions.")
H("690.d.1.C",3,"Repeating back what a user said, such as 'so the menu confused you?', is an example of:","active listening",["interrupting","multitasking","guessing"],"Paraphrasing confirms understanding.")
H("690.d.1.C",4,"Asking a follow-up question when a user's answer is unclear helps the designer to:","clarify the information received",["end the interview early","change the topic","avoid notes"],"Clarifying prevents misunderstandings.")
H("690.d.1.D",3,"A team designing a bank app should consider the viewpoints of both a teenager and a retired person because users can be:","diverse in age, ability and experience",["identical","unimportant","predictable in every way"],"Different users need different things.")
H("690.d.1.D",4,"Ignoring the viewpoint of users with low vision can result in a product that:","excludes people who cannot use it",["works for everyone","is automatically accessible","has fewer colors by law"],"Missing viewpoints creates barriers.")
H("690.d.1.E",3,"A UX designer who calmly explains design decisions to stakeholders and handles feedback politely is showing:","public relations skills",["coding speed","drawing speed","typing speed"],"PR skills build trust and support.")
H("690.d.1.E",4,"Sharing a project's progress in a clear newsletter to build excitement among stakeholders is an example of:","public relations in UX",["file compression","wire-framing","coding style"],"Communication builds support for design work.")
H("690.d.2.A",3,"A current challenge in the UX field is keeping designs accessible while:","new devices and screen sizes keep appearing",["avoiding all users","stopping research","refusing feedback"],"Devices keep multiplying.")
H("690.d.2.A",4,"A trend shaping UX is the growth of voice and gesture interfaces, which means designers must plan for:","interactions that do not use a mouse or touch screen",["only paper forms","only desktop monitors","only printed menus"],"New input modes expand UX.")
H("690.d.2.B",3,"A professional who studies how people use products through interviews and surveys is a:","UX researcher",["network cable","loan officer","pilot"],"Researchers gather user insight.")
H("690.d.2.B",4,"Career roles in UX range from researcher and interaction designer to:","content strategist and usability tester",["only coder","only janitor","only accountant"],"UX has many specialties.")
H("690.d.2.C",3,"The term 'user experience' describes:","how a person feels and what they do when using a product",["the price of a product","the weight of a device","the length of a manual"],"UX covers the whole interaction.")
H("690.d.2.C",4,"Human-centered design means designing with a strong focus on:","the needs and abilities of the people who will use it",["the cheapest materials","the designer's taste only","the fastest shipping"],"People come first.")
H("690.d.2.D",3,"A weather app that shows the forecast for your current location is:","relevant",["irrelevant","hostile","hidden"],"Relevant means it fits the user's need.")
H("690.d.2.D",4,"An experience that gets a task done quickly without confusion is best described as:","useful and friendly",["slow and cluttered","hidden and tricky","random and noisy"],"Useful helps; friendly is pleasant to use.")
H("690.d.2.E",3,"People tend to click the big, bright button first. This shows how behavior is influenced by:","visual attention and psychology",["luck","internet speed","paper quality"],"Psychology drives where people look and click.")
H("690.d.2.E",4,"A designer uses a familiar shopping-cart icon because users already expect it. This applies the idea that people rely on:","mental models from past experience",["random choice","slow typing","bright colors only"],"Familiar patterns reduce effort.")
H("690.d.2.F",3,"Design thinking begins by trying to understand users in a stage called:","empathize",["publish","sell","delete"],"Empathy is the first stage.")
H("690.d.2.F",4,"After brainstorming ideas, a design thinking team builds a quick model and then:","tests it with users and iterates",["ships it untested","stops working","hides the model"],"Prototype, test and refine.")
H("690.d.2.G",3,"A clear, easy-to-use ticket kiosk at a train station shows how UX design affects:","everyday lives",["only gamers","only engineers","only artists"],"Good UX makes daily tasks easier.")
H("690.d.2.G",4,"A confusing medication app could lead to mistakes, which shows that poor UX can affect:","people's safety and health",["only color choice","only logos","only fonts"],"UX has real-world consequences.")
H("690.d.3.A",3,"Ethical use of technology includes respecting others':","privacy and rights",["passwords for sharing","photos for selling","emails for forwarding"],"Ethics means respecting people.")
H("690.d.3.A",4,"A designer who tests a prototype with people should ethically get their:","informed consent",["bank details","home address","favorite food"],"Participants should agree knowingly.")
H("690.d.3.B",3,"For a student's original poem and drawing, copyright law protects:","original creative works such as art, writing and music",["any idea spoken aloud","simple facts only","public street names"],"Copyright covers expression.")
H("690.d.3.B",4,"A trademark protects a brand's name or logo, while a patent protects:","an invention",["a recipe name","a color scheme only","a font style only"],"Patents cover new inventions.")
H("690.d.3.C",3,"A designer copies a photographer's picture into a client site without permission. This is:","copyright infringement",["fair design","brand building","a patent right"],"Using without permission infringes.")
H("690.d.3.C",4,"Selling shoes with a logo that looks almost identical to a famous brand's logo may violate:","trademark law",["gravity","patent law only","copyright law only"],"Confusingly similar marks are infringement.")
H("690.d.3.D",3,"A student caught plagiarizing may face:","a failing grade or other disciplinary action",["a prize","a promotion","a free upgrade"],"Plagiarism has consequences.")
H("690.d.3.D",4,"For a professional designer, plagiarism could also lead to:","lost clients and legal action",["better reviews","higher pay","new patents"],"Reputation and law are at risk.")
H("690.d.3.E",3,"Using a quotation from a website in a research report requires:","a proper citation",["a new logo","hiding the source","deleting quotation marks"],"Citing credits the author.")
H("690.d.3.E",4,"When using an online photo, ethical practice is to check its license and:","give credit as required",["claim it as your own","remove the creator's name","resell it"],"Follow license terms.")
H("690.d.4.A",3,"Qualitative data describes experiences in words, such as:","comments users make in interviews",["the number of clicks","the time in seconds","the percent of users"],"Qualitative = descriptive.")
H("690.d.4.A",4,"Quantitative data can be measured and counted, such as:","the percent of users who finished checkout",["a user's feelings described in a story","a user's quote about frustration","an interview recording"],"Quantitative = numbers.")
H("690.d.4.B",3,"In a user interview, a good question is open-ended, like:","'Tell me about the last time you used this site.'",["'You liked it, right?'","'Is it good, yes or no?'","'Don't you think the menu is clear?'"],"Open questions invite detail.")
H("690.d.4.B",4,"A leading question such as 'Don't you love this feature?' should be avoided because it:","pushes the user toward a particular answer",["gets honest, unbiased answers","gets longer stories","improves research quality"],"Leading questions bias results.")
H("690.d.4.C",3,"A designer groups sticky-note ideas from interviews on a digital board to:","find patterns in the feedback",["print posters","delete data","hide notes"],"Organizing reveals themes.")
H("690.d.4.C",4,"Tagging interview notes in a spreadsheet by theme such as 'navigation' or 'checkout' makes it easier to:","spot repeated problems",["lose the notes","double the workload","avoid analysis"],"Tags surface patterns.")
H("690.d.4.D",3,"Five of six interviewed users say they could not find the search box. A reasonable conclusion is:","the search box is hard to find",["users love search","the site is perfect","interviews are useless"],"Repeated feedback signals a problem.")
H("690.d.4.D",4,"When analyzing interview data, a designer should avoid:","jumping to conclusions from one comment",["looking for patterns","checking multiple users","taking notes"],"One comment is not a pattern.")
H("690.d.4.E",3,"In a task analysis observation, a researcher watches a user try to complete a task such as:","booking a library room online",["reading a book at home","buying clothes without the site","sleeping"],"Observation shows real behavior.")
H("690.d.4.E",4,"During an observation, the researcher should document where the user pauses, makes errors and:","what they say while working",["what the researcher likes","the researcher's guesses","unrelated news"],"Behavior and comments both matter.")
H("690.d.4.F",3,"An affinity map groups similar findings together so a team can see:","themes in the research",["the budget","the schedule","the paint colors"],"Affinity maps cluster related notes.")
H("690.d.4.F",4,"A customer journey map shows the steps a person takes and how they:","feel at each step",["pay taxes","write code","mix colors"],"Journey maps combine actions and emotions.")
H("690.d.4.G",3,"A persona is a fictional user profile based on:","patterns found in real research",["a designer's random guess","a celebrity","nothing at all"],"Personas summarize real data.")
H("690.d.4.G",4,"A persona usually includes goals, needs and:","frustrations",["a social security number","a bank balance","a medical record"],"Pain points guide design.")
H("690.d.4.H",3,"A research report should present interview and observation data using:","clear summaries and visuals",["raw unorganized notes only","jargon only","blank slides"],"Summaries make findings usable.")
H("690.d.4.H",4,"After reporting findings, a designer should end the presentation with:","recommendations based on the data",["jokes only","a blank slide","unrelated opinions"],"Insights should lead to action.")
H("690.d.5.A",3,"Balance, contrast and alignment are examples of:","design principles",["server settings","file types","coding bugs"],"They guide how elements are arranged.")
H("690.d.5.A",4,"Using large text for headings and small text for details helps show:","visual hierarchy",["random layout","hidden menus","broken links"],"Hierarchy ranks importance.")
H("690.d.5.B",3,"A visceral reaction to a design is a person's:","immediate, gut-level response to how it looks and feels",["slow, detailed analysis","written report","technical audit"],"Visceral responses are instant.")
H("690.d.5.B",4,"A clean, attractive welcome screen that makes users feel good in the first seconds builds:","a positive first impression",["slower loading","less trust","more confusion"],"First impressions affect experience.")
H("690.d.5.C",3,"Red is often used for warnings and errors because people tend to associate it with:","danger or urgency",["calm and sleep","nature and growth","coldness and ice"],"Color carries meaning.")
H("690.d.5.C",4,"A meditation app would likely choose soft blues and greens to encourage:","a calm mood",["urgency and panic","aggression","alarm"],"Color influences emotion.")
H("690.d.5.D",3,"Many readers scan a web page in an F-shaped pattern, so designers put key information:","near the top and left",["at the very bottom","in hidden menus","in tiny text"],"Scanning patterns guide layout.")
H("690.d.5.D",4,"Because people scan rather than read every word, designers use clear headings and short:","paragraphs and bullet lists",["unbroken walls of text","tiny fonts","dense tables only"],"Scannable content helps users.")
H("690.d.5.E",3,"Hick's Law says that the more choices a person has, the longer it takes them to:","make a decision",["blink","walk","sleep"],"More options slow decisions.")
H("690.d.5.E",4,"Weber's Law states that people notice a change based on its size relative to the original. So a tiny change to a very large price:","may go unnoticed",["is always obvious","is always rejected","is illegal"],"Noticeability is proportional.")
H("690.d.5.F",3,"After a while, you stop noticing a steady background hum. This is called:","sensory adaptation",["hearing loss","a bug","a network error"],"Senses adapt to constant stimuli.")
H("690.d.5.F",4,"A perceptual set is the tendency to perceive things based on:","expectations and past experience",["screen size","file size","font size"],"Expectations shape perception.")
H("690.d.5.G",3,"In human information processing, taking in information through the eyes and ears is the stage of:","sensing",["deciding","responding","forgetting"],"Sensing is the first stage.")
H("690.d.5.G",4,"After sensing, the brain interprets what was sensed in the stage called:","perceiving",["sleeping","printing","charging"],"Perceiving interprets sensory input.")
H("690.d.6.A",3,"Watching how nurses actually use a patient-record screen on a busy ward helps identify:","real-world problems and needs",["new logo ideas","office furniture","computer brands"],"Context reveals true needs.")
H("690.d.6.A",4,"A designer asks bus riders why they skip the trip-planning app and learns they have no signal underground. The need identified is:","reliable use without internet",["a brighter screen","more ads","smaller buttons"],"Needs emerge from real conditions.")
H("690.d.6.B",3,"The accessibility principle 'perceivable' means users must be able to:","sense the content, for example by seeing or hearing it",["buy it","print it","steal it"],"Content must be presentable to senses.")
H("690.d.6.B",4,"Making sure a site can be used with only a keyboard supports which accessibility principle?","operable",["perceivable","profitable","portable"],"Operable means usable with various controls.")
H("690.d.6.C",3,"UX design focuses on the whole experience, while visual design focuses mainly on:","the look and style of the interface",["the database","the network","the budget"],"Visual design is the appearance.")
H("690.d.6.C",4,"Interaction design, a part of UX, deals with:","how users and a product respond to each other",["only color choices","only server speed","only printing"],"Interaction design shapes behavior flows.")
H("690.d.6.D",3,"A designer presents a user's problem as a short story about a person's day to help the team:","feel empathy and understand the need",["skip research","hide the user","avoid prototypes"],"Stories make needs vivid.")
H("690.d.6.D",4,"Storytelling in a design pitch works best when it links the user's problem to:","the proposed solution",["the designer's lunch","random facts","the company's party"],"A story should lead to the idea.")
H("690.d.6.E",3,"A wireframe is a simple layout that shows:","where content and controls will go",["final colors and photos","finished code","user salaries"],"Wireframes outline structure.")
H("690.d.6.E",4,"A prototype differs from a wireframe in that a prototype can:","simulate how a user would move through the design",["only show boxes","only show text","only be printed"],"Prototypes are interactive.")
H("690.d.6.F",3,"A structured usability test uses the same set of tasks for each participant so results can be:","compared fairly",["ignored","hidden","guessed"],"Consistency enables comparison.")
H("690.d.6.F",4,"After a test shows that users miss a button, the designer makes a change and tests again. This is called:","iteration",["abandonment","plagiarism","deletion"],"Iterating improves the design.")
H("690.d.7.A",3,"UX research feeds into design thinking by providing:","evidence about what users need",["random opinions","extra file formats","decorations"],"Research informs each stage.")
H("690.d.7.A",4,"The 'define' stage of design thinking uses research to state:","the problem to solve",["the price","the slogan","the schedule"],"Research findings define the problem.")
H("690.d.7.B",3,"A project manager uses a method like Agile in UX projects to work in:","short cycles with regular feedback",["one giant step","secret phases","random order"],"Agile uses sprints.")
H("690.d.7.B",4,"In many UX project methods, stages such as research, design and testing are handled by team members with different:","roles",["passwords","phones","desk colors"],"Roles divide responsibility.")
H("690.d.8.A",3,"Typeface, color, shape, texture, space and form are all:","design elements",["server types","HTML tags","legal terms"],"They are building blocks of visual design.")
H("690.d.8.A",4,"Choosing a rounded, friendly style of lettering for a kids' app uses the design element of:","typeface",["texture only","audio","video"],"Fonts set tone.")
H("690.d.8.B",3,"A page where headings, images and text feel like they belong together shows the principle of:","unity",["clutter","chaos","randomness"],"Unity makes elements cohere.")
H("690.d.8.B",4,"Making the most important button larger than the others uses the principle of:","scale and hierarchy",["noise","delay","speed"],"Size signals importance.")
H("690.d.8.C",3,"In HTML, the element used to create a hyperlink is:","<a>",["<p>","<h1>","<br>"],"The anchor tag makes links.")
H("690.d.8.C",4,"The HTML element used for the largest heading on a page is:","<h1>",["<a>","<img>","<ul>"],"h1 is the top-level heading.")
H("690.d.8.E",3,"Quick, rough sketches of an interface help a designer to:","explore ideas fast before using software",["finalize the code","pay taxes","install updates"],"Sketching is cheap exploration.")
H("690.d.8.E",4,"A designer sketches five different layouts for a home screen to:","compare options before choosing one",["delay the project","avoid feedback","use more paper for no reason"],"Variety supports choice.")
H("690.d.8.F",3,"Design software used to create wireframes lets a designer drag and place:","boxes, text and buttons on a canvas",["real servers","physical bricks","tax forms"],"Tools place interface elements.")
H("690.d.8.F",4,"Reusable components in wireframing software, like a navigation bar, help keep screens:","consistent and quicker to build",["slower to change","random","incomplete"],"Components save time.")
H("690.d.8.G",3,"Design fidelity describes how close a design is to the:","final product",["first idea in someone's head","office layout","budget"],"Fidelity measures realism.")
H("690.d.8.G",4,"Moving from sketch to wireframe to prototype to visuals gradually:","adds detail and realism",["removes all detail","hides the design","deletes the project"],"Fidelity increases step by step.")
H("690.d.8.H",3,"Digital assets for a website include images, icons and:","fonts and logos",["office keys","coffee cups","parking passes"],"Assets are files used in the design.")
H("690.d.8.H",4,"Exporting an icon in several sizes for different screens is part of:","producing digital assets",["writing a contract","painting a wall","repairing hardware"],"Assets must fit varied devices.")
H("690.d.8.D.i",3,"Browser-based interfaces must work across different:","screen sizes and browsers",["paper sizes","car models","power outlets"],"Responsive design handles variety.")
H("690.d.8.D.i",4,"A mobile interface usually puts navigation where a user's thumb can reach it because:","phones are often held and used with one hand",["phones have no screens","thumbs are unused","keyboards are required"],"Ergonomics guide mobile layout.")
H("690.d.8.D.ii",3,"A vector graphic is made from:","mathematical lines and shapes that scale cleanly",["only pixels","only sounds","only text files"],"Vectors scale without blur.")
H("690.d.8.D.ii",4,"A photograph is best stored as a raster image because it:","contains detailed color changes in pixels",["is drawn only with lines","has no color","is a math formula"],"Rasters capture photographic detail.")
H("690.d.8.D.iii",3,"The front end of a website is the part that:","users see and interact with",["stays hidden in the database","only the server uses","only the programmer sees"],"Front end is the interface.")
H("690.d.8.D.iii",4,"The back end of a website handles things like:","storing data and running server logic",["choosing fonts","painting buttons","drawing icons"],"Back end works behind the scenes.")
H("690.d.8.D.iv",3,"A basic web page with links and graphics needs HTML for structure and an image tag to:","display the graphic",["send an email","print the page","play a game"],"Images are embedded with markup.")
H("690.d.8.D.iv",4,"To make a graphic on a page open another page when clicked, the designer wraps the image in a:","link (anchor element)",["heading","table","comment"],"Linked images use anchors.")

# ---- 691 User Experience (UX) Design II ----
H("691.d.2",3,"A designer applies the idea of empathy from class by interviewing real commuters about a transit app. This connects:","a conceptual foundation to a real-world project",["a font to a color","a bug to a feature","a price to a logo"],"Foundations are applied to real users.")
H("691.d.2",4,"A student connects the principle of consistency to a real redesign by making sure buttons:","look and behave the same on every screen",["change style on every page","hide on some screens","use random labels"],"Consistency is a foundation applied in practice.")
H("691.d.1.A",3,"A client's website uses a famous brand's logo without permission. The designer should identify this as an:","intellectual property violation",["accessibility feature","color choice","layout pattern"],"Unlicensed logos violate rights.")
H("691.d.1.A",4,"A teammate suggests copying a competitor's unique icon set exactly. A designer recognizes the risk of:","copyright infringement",["better branding","faster loading","stronger contrast"],"Copying protected art is infringement.")
H("691.d.1.B",3,"A designer explains to a client the ramifications of using unlicensed photos, such as:","legal costs and damage to reputation",["higher traffic","better colors","faster pages"],"Violations carry consequences.")
H("691.d.1.B",4,"A designer may communicate ramifications of an IP violation visually, orally or in writing, but the message should always be:","clear and accurate",["vague","misleading","secret"],"Accurate communication guides decisions.")
H("691.d.3.A",3,"The stages of the UX design process include research, identifying problems, ideating, prototyping and:","testing",["guessing","hiding","printing"],"Testing follows prototyping.")
H("691.d.3.A",4,"The stage in which a designer defines the specific problem to solve comes right after:","research",["launch","maintenance","billing"],"Research informs problem definition.")
H("691.d.3.B",3,"Testing a half-finished prototype early lets a designer:","find problems before spending more time building",["avoid users","skip design","delay all work"],"Early tests save effort.")
H("691.d.3.B",4,"Results from a partial-product test showing users get lost in the menu should lead the designer to:","revise the navigation",["ignore the test","remove the testers","finish the code first"],"Findings drive revisions.")
H("691.d.3.C",3,"A content strategy plans what content a site needs and:","how it will be created and organized",["the length of the sales team","the paper stock","the keyboard type"],"Strategy covers content planning.")
H("691.d.3.C",4,"Getting feedback from stakeholders and users on a conceptual design helps a team to:","confirm direction before building details",["avoid all decisions","remove the design","skip research"],"Early feedback reduces rework.")
H("691.d.3.D",3,"Breaking a design project into tasks with due dates is an example of:","time management and planning",["font selection","image compression","server setup"],"Planning keeps projects on schedule.")
H("691.d.3.D",4,"A designer finds that user testing will take longer than planned and tells the team early so they can:","adjust the schedule",["hide the delay","cancel testing","miss the deadline silently"],"Early communication helps rescheduling.")
H("691.d.4.A",3,"A questionnaire template saves time because it can be:","reused for similar research studies",["thrown away","used once only","printed on posters"],"Templates make research efficient.")
H("691.d.4.A",4,"A summary report template should include sections for goals, method, findings and:","recommendations",["recipes","lyrics","jokes"],"Reports end with next steps.")
H("691.d.4.B",3,"A project summary that includes insights from the data should connect each conclusion to:","evidence from the research",["a personal hunch","a coin flip","a rumor"],"Conclusions need evidence.")
H("691.d.4.B",4,"If survey scores and interview comments both point to confusing checkout steps, the designer's summary should highlight:","that consistent finding",["only the best comment","only the worst score","nothing"],"Converging evidence is strong.")
H("691.d.4.C",3,"Qualitative research methods such as user interviews and field studies collect:","detailed descriptions of behavior and opinions",["only counts","only prices","only server logs"],"Qualitative = rich description.")
H("691.d.4.C",4,"A diary study, where users record their daily experiences with a product, is a:","qualitative method",["quantitative method","hardware test","legal review"],"Diary studies yield descriptive data.")
H("691.d.4.D",3,"A/B testing compares two versions of a page to see which:","performs better with real users",["costs less to print","has more pages","is longer"],"A/B tests compare variants.")
H("691.d.4.D",4,"A heat map of clicks on a page shows:","where users click most often",["how long the code is","who wrote the page","where the server is"],"Heat maps visualize interaction.")
H("691.d.5.A",3,"Users keep abandoning their carts at the shipping-cost page. The UX problem is:","unexpected costs appearing late in checkout",["a wrong font","too many photos","a slow printer"],"Problems are specific and observable.")
H("691.d.5.A",4,"After naming a UX problem, the next step is to list:","possible solutions",["new logos","staff birthdays","email addresses"],"Solutions follow problem identification.")
H("691.d.5.B",3,"To evaluate possible solutions, a designer compares them against user needs, cost and:","feasibility",["font size only","paper weight","brand slogans"],"Feasibility affects choices.")
H("691.d.5.B",4,"An action plan for a chosen solution lists tasks, owners and:","deadlines",["wallpapers","lunch menus","parking spots"],"Plans assign time and responsibility.")
H("691.d.5.C",3,"A presentable content strategy might include a site map and a plan for:","what content goes on each page",["employee schedules","hardware pricing","office decor"],"Strategy organizes content.")
H("691.d.5.C",4,"Symbolic designs such as icons and logos should be tested to see whether users:","understand what they mean",["like their color only","can print them","can sell them"],"Symbols must be recognizable.")
H("691.d.5.D",3,"Brainstorming with no judging of ideas at first is a method called:","unstructured ideation",["final review","budget approval","code review"],"Open discussion generates many ideas.")
H("691.d.5.D",4,"A structured ideation method where each person sketches six quick ideas in a short time is called:","a rapid sketching session",["a marathon","an audit","a data entry"],"Rapid sketches produce variety fast.")
H("691.d.5.E",3,"A people-centered rationale for choosing an idea explains how the idea:","meets users' needs",["is cheapest for the designer","looks trendy","matches the CEO's taste only"],"Rationales tie ideas to users.")
H("691.d.5.E",4,"Selecting ideas for prototyping should include input from users or team members to:","avoid personal bias",["delay decisions","reduce testing","hide ideas"],"Group input balances bias.")
H("691.d.5.F",3,"A low-fidelity prototype such as a paper sketch is useful because it is:","quick and cheap to change",["expensive","permanent","fully coded"],"Low-fi allows fast iteration.")
H("691.d.5.F",4,"A click-through prototype made of images linked together lets testers:","tap through a simulated flow",["write final code","print business cards","hire staff"],"Click-throughs simulate navigation.")
H("691.d.5.G",3,"A high-fidelity prototype looks and behaves:","very close to the final product",["like a rough doodle","like a blank page","like a paper note"],"High-fi feels real.")
H("691.d.5.G",4,"A physical prototype of a smart-watch case, 3D printed to test fit, is a:","high-fidelity physical mockup",["wireframe in software","list of tasks","budget form"],"Physical models test form.")
H("691.d.6.A",3,"Page layouts, content blocks, visual design and navigation must work together to create:","a coherent user experience",["a random page","a slower server","extra ads"],"Elements connect into one experience.")
H("691.d.6.A",4,"If navigation labels do not match the headings on the pages they open, the connected experience becomes:","confusing for users",["clearer","faster","more secure"],"Mismatches break flow.")
H("691.d.6.B",3,"Designers must distinguish channels such as web, mobile app and email because each:","has different formats and user expectations",["has the same rules","needs no design","has no users"],"Channels vary.")
H("691.d.6.B",4,"A message designed for a wide desktop page may need to be reformatted for a narrow:","phone screen",["printer","fax","router"],"Format must fit the channel.")
H("691.d.6.C",3,"A co-creation workshop invites users to:","help design the solution with the team",["watch only","stay away","approve the final paper"],"Co-creation involves users.")
H("691.d.6.C",4,"A peer-review activity helps a designer by providing:","critique from fellow designers",["free hardware","legal advice","payment"],"Peers give constructive feedback.")
H("691.d.6.D",3,"Comparing a site's navigation test results with those of competitors helps a team to:","see where their design is stronger or weaker",["copy their logos","ignore users","stop testing"],"Benchmarking informs improvement.")
H("691.d.6.D",4,"A navigation test asks users to find an item, and the designer records the time and number of:","wrong clicks",["pixels","fonts","emails"],"Errors reveal friction.")
H("691.d.6.E",3,"Including the designer's own voice in documentation means:","explaining reasoning in the designer's own words",["copying other authors","hiding the source","using no sources"],"Voice shows understanding.")
H("691.d.6.E",4,"Best practices for references in a design report include:","listing sources so readers can find them",["omitting sources","using only rumors","hiding authors"],"References support credibility.")
H("691.d.7.A",3,"A usability test plan should list goals, tasks, participants and:","the success measures",["the cafeteria menu","staff salaries","unrelated news"],"Plans define how success is measured.")
H("691.d.7.A",4,"A plan that tests cognitive, perceptual, emotional and physical factors makes sure the test looks at:","how thinking, seeing, feeling and handling affect use",["only the color red","only server speed","only price"],"These dimensions cover human factors.")
H("691.d.7.B",3,"When running a usability test, the moderator should avoid:","helping or hinting while the user works",["taking notes","recording sessions","giving instructions"],"Hints bias results.")
H("691.d.7.B",4,"Collecting data during testing includes task completion rates, time on task and:","user comments",["staff opinions only","unrelated stats","none"],"Mix of numbers and comments.")
H("691.d.7.C",3,"Conclusions from a usability test should be presented with recommendations that apply:","design principles and are backed by data",["personal guesses","random ideas","unrelated trends"],"Evidence plus principles.")
H("691.d.7.C",4,"Clear communication of test results to stakeholders makes it more likely that the team will:","act on the recommendations",["ignore the findings","delay the project","cancel testing"],"Clarity drives action.")

B.balance()
B.save(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "..", "batches", "cte_88.jsonl"))
